Scenario A stock split changes the shares and the price but posts nothing
Description The value of the holding is the same before and after, so there is
Description nothing to post, and posting a revaluation of zero would clutter
Description the register. The Q field holds the number of new shares for each
Description old one, multiplied by ten, which is Quicken's own convention.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-02-01 |
Given the file contains
"""
!Type:Invst
D03/01/2024
NStkSplit
YVTSAX
Q20
^
"""
When qif file imported
Then postings created are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date | Account | Amount |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price   | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 200    | 50.0000 | 2024-03-01 |

BusinessRule How a stock split ratio is read
Description The Q field is the new shares per old share, times ten.
Details This is the convention Quicken writes and it is worth confirming
Details against the file being migrated, because a wrong reading here changes
Details a share count by a factor of ten.
Examples: SplitRatio
| QField | Ratio | HeldBefore | HeldAfter | PriceBefore | PriceAfter | Notes       |
| 20     | 2     | 100        | 200       | 100.0000    | 50.0000    | Two for one |
| 30     | 3     | 100        | 300       | 120.0000    | 40.0000    | Three for one |
| 15     | 1.5   | 100        | 150       | 90.0000     | 60.0000    | Three for two |
| 5      | 0.5   | 100        | 50        | 50.0000     | 100.0000   | A reverse split |

Attributes SplitRatio
| Attribute   | Type    | Default |
| QField      | Decimal | 0       |
| Ratio       | Decimal | 0       |
| HeldBefore  | Shares  | 0       |
| HeldAfter   | Shares  | 0       |
| PriceBefore | Price   | 0       |
| PriceAfter  | Price   | 0       |
| Notes       | String  | none    |

Scenario An unsupported action is reported and not imported
Description Employee stock plan actions carry tax meaning this program does not
Description model. Importing them as something else would be worse than
Description leaving them out and saying so.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given the file contains
"""
!Type:Invst
D03/01/2024
NVest
YOld Employer Stock Plan
Q50
^
"""
When qif file imported
Then postings created are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date | Account | Amount |
Then migration notes are : MigrationNote
| Kind        | Detail                                            |
| Unsupported | 2024-03-01 action "Vest" is not imported; 1 record |

