| TransactionsChecked | Integer | 0       |
| OutOfBalance        | Integer | 0       |
| Balanced            | Boolean | false   |

Scenario Importing the same QIF file twice does not double the book
Description A migration gets run again: because the first attempt was abandoned,
Description or because a second export was taken. Every record carries a
Description fingerprint of its account, date, amount, payee and category, and
Description a record whose fingerprint is already present is offered rather
Description than created, as a CSV row is in ImportCsv.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Assets:Checking |
Given the file contains
"""
!Type:Bank
D01/15/2024
T-45.00
PHarris Teeter
LGroceries
^
"""
When qif file imported
Then import summary is : ImportSummary Vertical
| New       | 1 |
| Duplicate | 0 |
| Matched   | 0 |
| Possible  | 0 |
When qif file imported
Then import summary is : ImportSummary Vertical
| New       | 0 |
| Duplicate | 0 |
| Matched   | 0 |
| Possible  | 1 |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the first round imports, and what it leaves
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description The first round is about spending reports from banking and card
Description accounts. This section says exactly which records that includes,
Description because the answer is not quite "the bank and card sections".

BusinessRule Which sections the first round imports
Description Every section that carries dated, categorised transactions, which is
Description more than the bank and card ones.
Details The invoice and bill sections are not investment data and not an aside:
Details across the two files they carry 334 income references and 660 expense
Details references. They are consulting revenue and business costs, and a
Details spending report without them is short by that much. They have the same
Details shape as a bank record -- a date, an amount, a payee, a category,
Details sometimes splits -- so they are imported the same way, and only their
Details X and A extension fields are dropped.
Details The securities side of the investment sections is the one thing left
Details out. See the rule after this one.
Examples: RoundOneSection
| Section        | Records | InRound1 | Why                                      |
| !Type:Bank     | 11,587  | true     | The main case                            |
| !Type:CCard    | 28,970  | true     | The main case                            |
| !Type:Cash     | 695     | true     | Same shape                               |
| !Type:Oth A    | 80      | true     | Same shape                               |
| !Type:Oth L    | 8       | true     | Same shape                               |
| !Type:Invoice  | 588     | true     | Carries income and expense categories    |
| !Type:Bill     | 68      | true     | Carries expense categories               |
| !Type:Tax      | 2       | true     | One record each; a transfer              |
| !Type:Cat      | 588     | true     | Needed to know income from expense       |
| !Type:Tag      | 2       | true     | Read; tags are kept but not reported on  |
| !Type:Memorized | 50     | true     | Becomes payee rules                      |
| !Type:Invst    | 899     | true     | Only the 51 with a category or transfer; see the next rule |
| !Type:InvItem  | 10      | false    | Invoice line items; nothing to post      |
| !Type:Template | 5       | false    | A report definition, not data            |

Attributes RoundOneSection
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Section   | String  |         |
| Records   | String  |         |
| InRound1  | Boolean | true    |
| Why       | String  | none    |

BusinessRule Which investment records the first round imports
Description Those that move cash to somewhere outside the account, and no
Description others. The securities side is left for a later round.
Details The reason this is not simply "skip the investment sections" is that
Details 21 of those records name a category that a spending report shows:
Details twenty use Investment transfer, which the category list declares as
Details income, and one uses Misc Expense. Dropping them would leave two
Details lines short against Quicken.
Details The other 848 records are dividends reinvested, buys, sells, shares in
Details and out, and the one stock split. None of them carries a category --
Details the holdings are in retirement accounts, so nothing they earn is
Details reportable spending or income -- and all of them are internal to the
Details account. Leaving them out changes no figure in a spending report.
Examples: RoundOneInvestmentAction
| Action   | Records | InRound1 | Becomes                                   |
| XIn      | 11      | true     | Cash in, from the account or category in L |
| XOut     | 8       | true     | Cash out, to the account or category in L  |
| Cash     | 41      | true     | A cash movement against the category in L  |
| Buy      | 74      | false    | Internal to the account; no category        |
| Sell     | 33      | false    | Internal; any gain is not reported          |
| ReinvDiv | 665     | false    | Retirement account; not reportable income   |
| Div      | 15      | false    | Likewise; carries no category               |
| ShrsIn   | 40      | false    | Shares from before the file                 |
| ShrsOut  | 11      | false    | Internal                                    |
| StkSplit | 1       | false    | No value changes                            |

Attributes RoundOneInvestmentAction
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Action    | String  |         |
| Records   | String  |         |
| InRound1  | Boolean | true    |
| Becomes   | String  |         |

Scenario An investment account exists so that a transfer into it stays a transfer
Description Nineteen banking and card records transfer to an investment account.
Description If the account did not exist those nineteen would fall to
Description Uncategorized, and money moved to a retirement account would read as
Description spending. So the accounts are created even though their contents are
Description not imported.
Given the qif profile is : QifProfile Vertical
| DateOrder      | MDY      |
| InvestmentMode | CashOnly |
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type    | Placeholder |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense | false       |
Given the file contains
