# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Invoices, and when their income is recognised
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description Income from an invoice is recognised when the invoice is paid, not
Description when it is issued. The reports being compared against are on a cash
Description basis, and that is what cash basis means.
Details
Details This section says what the QIF export makes possible, which is less than
Details the rule asks for, and it says so rather than approximating quietly.

BusinessRule How the invoice section is shaped
Description Two kinds of record share the section, told apart by the L field.
Details Observed in the business file: 425 records, 212 invoices and 213
Details payments. The counts are almost equal because almost every invoice was
Details paid.
Examples: InvoiceRecordKind
| Kind    | LField           | HasSplitLines | CarriesCategories | Count |
| Invoice | --Split--        | true          | true              | 207   |
| Invoice | An income category | false       | true              | 5     |
| Payment | A bracketed account | false      | false             | 213   |

Attributes InvoiceRecordKind
| Attribute         | Type    | Default |
| Kind              | String  |         |
| LField            | String  |         |
| HasSplitLines     | Boolean | false   |
| CarriesCategories | Boolean | false   |
| Count             | String  |         |

BusinessRule The export does not say which payment paid which invoice
Description So a payment cannot be given the categories of its invoice with
Description certainty, and that is the obstacle to posting income at the payment
Description date.
Details The evidence, all from the business file:
Details Not one of the 213 payment records carries a split line, so no payment
Details names a category of its own.
Details The only field that looked like a reference, XI, has two distinct values
Details across all 425 records -- 1 and 3 -- so it is a record-type flag and
Details not an identifier. XE is a due date and X# is a quantity.
Details Matching on payee and amount, oldest invoice first, resolves 184 of the
Details 213 payments exactly. A payee-only fallback reaches about 204. The
Details remainder are partial payments, combined payments, or payments whose
Details payee was edited.
Details That residual is not good enough to post income from, because a
Details comparison that has to agree to the cent cannot rest on a match that
Details is right most of the time.
Examples: InvoiceLinkEvidence
| Question                                | Answer                                  |
| Do payments carry categories            | No; 0 of 213 have split lines           |
| Is there a reference field              | No; XI has 2 distinct values over 425 records |
| Does payee and amount recover the link  | Partly; 184 of 213 exactly              |
| Is that enough to post income from      | No                                      |

Attributes InvoiceLinkEvidence
| Attribute | Type   | Default |
| Question  | String |         |
| Answer    | String |         |

BusinessRule How a payment is matched to the invoice it paid
Description In three passes, and whatever is left over is reported rather than
Description attached to something by guesswork.
Details The link is not in the export, so it is reconstructed. Pass one is
Details exact and settles most of it; pass two accepts a different amount from
Details the same payee, which is a partial or combined payment; pass three
Details gives up and says so.
Details On the business file: 184 of 213 payments match exactly, 20 more match a
Details payee with some invoice still open, and 9 match nothing at all.
Examples: PaymentMatchPass
| Pass | Rule                                                        | Matched |
| 1    | Same payee and the same amount, oldest invoice first        | 184     |
| 2    | Same payee, any open invoice, oldest first                  | 20      |
| 3    | Nothing; the payment is reported and posted uncategorised    | 9       |

Attributes PaymentMatchPass
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Pass      | Integer | 0       |
| Rule      | String  |         |
| Matched   | String  |         |

Scenario Income posts at the payment date, not the invoice date
Description The invoice is dated November 2025 and was paid in January 2026. On
Description a cash basis the income is 2026 income, so the categories of the
Description invoice are posted on the day the money arrived.
Details The invoice itself posts nothing. It is the record of what the income
Details is for, and it is held until a payment claims it.
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Assets:Customer Invoices |
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                     | Type   | Placeholder |
| Assets:Customer Invoices | Asset  | false       |
| Assets:Checking          | Bank   | false       |
| Income:Consulting        | Income | false       |
